# Commit the curated memory; ignore raw model traffic and machine-local state.
#
# From logs/, one thing goes to git:
#   runs.jsonl    the run records — provenance for every reported number
#
# Everything else here is working material, not memory. The briefs sent to each
# debate seat and the full model responses are both inputs to a decision, and a
# coauthor asking "did we ever explore X" wants the decision and the reason for
# it, not the prompts that produced it. That answer belongs in the state's
# changelog, written when the decision is made — see the debate section of
# CLAUDE.md. Raw material nobody curated reads as a record and is not one.
#
# The style-capture buffer lands here too — style-observations.jsonl,
# style-prompts.json, style-watermark — and stays local for the same reason,
# plus one of its own: those are the passages one coauthor was corrected on.
# What gets shared is the rule someone accepted, written into writing-guide.md
# at the repo root, which IS committed.
#
# Note the rule shape: git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is
# ignored, so this must be `*/logs/*` plus a negation, never `*/logs/`.
*/logs/*
!*/logs/runs.jsonl

# Per-author runtime state: machine-local, and meaningless to anyone else.
# `python` in particular holds an absolute venv path.
*/run
*/python

# machine-local: this clone has been through onboarding
*/onboarded
